      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T13:45:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about DT reserved-memory nodes without `no-map`? Shouldn\u0027t we insert resources for them as well? https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20180723015732.24252-2-takahiro.akashi@linaro.org/\n\nCan we instead reuse `reserve_region_with_split()` somehow, like arm64 does?\n\nOr maybe what we should actually do is to update e820, before inserting resources, like we do in `e820__reserve_setup_data()`, for example?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "2643cc4e_b68e8979",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kernel/e820.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1204,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1207,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\tstart \u003d __pfn_to_phys(memblock_region_reserved_base_pfn(region));\n\t\tend \u003d __pfn_to_phys(memblock_region_reserved_end_pfn(region)) - 1;\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kernel/e820.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 1208,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 1212,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\t/* If overlaps with existing region, rearrange resources */\n\t\tif (start \u003c\u003d e820_res-\u003eend \u0026\u0026 end \u003e\u003d e820_res-\u003estart) {\n\t\t\tsplit_resource(e820_res, start, end);\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "4cec988fea52cc9bdd28f42ca71d825e6e0cf374",
